{"chapter": "sets", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "000H", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\text{size}(S) = \\max(\\aleph_0, \\kappa_1, \\kappa_2),\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$\\kappa_1$", "MATH_0004": "$\\kappa_2$", "MATH_0005": "$\\kappa_1$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$\\kappa_2$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Gamma(U, \\mathcal{O}_S)$", "MATH_0009": "$U \\subset S$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:425be2c5ac30aa622ae1cefab821038f7d932fd46169027cfcaa13cb5a684fe7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5fd8bc0852ffa7e87bde65282f56b9c06ac123e9518d9f72808de2fe33889c33", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe will discuss how to apply this to produce, given an initial\nset of schemes, a ``small'' category of schemes closed under\na list of natural operations. Before we do so, we introduce the\nsize of a scheme. Given a scheme <MATH_0001> we define\n<MATH_0002>\nwhere we define the cardinal numbers <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004> as follows:\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> We let <MATH_0005> be the cardinality of the set of affine opens of <MATH_0006>.\n<STRUCT_0004> We let <MATH_0007> be the supremum of all the cardinalities of\nall <MATH_0008> for all <MATH_0009> affine open.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cdca09b3c87ff692b4e1821177b71bb22a04ede16bc817d3e3c0536c9710838f", "unit_id": "tag:000H:prose-0001"}
